  "equivalent_all_d_dimensional_form": "F_r int(-1/4 Fbar^2) = F_r int(-1/4 F^2) + F_r Etilde_F^(r); -Yt |Dbar H|^2 = -Yt |D H|^2 - Yt Etilde_H. Then delta S = (all d-dim invariant directions) + Etilde_F^(r) [-2/3 S_F^(r)] + Etilde_H [-Yt] + E_A^(r) [-1/3 S_F^(r)] + E_H [-2/3 Yt].",
  "b_d_of_delta_S": "b_d O_A^(r,d) = 0, b_d (O_g - O_c)^(r,d) = 0, b_d O_c^(r,d) = b_d O_g^(r,d) = Delta_1^(r) (the part of eq:Delta1 with ghosts of factor r), barred invariants, Etilde_F, Etilde_H, O_psi, O_H^(d), Q_lambda, Q_m, Q^+ are b_d-closed. Hence b_d delta S^(1) = kappa [ sum_(r=G,W) (K_r + Gamma_r) Delta_1^(r) + sum_r c_EA^(r) b_d E_A^(r) + c_EH b_d E_H ], K_r + Gamma_r = -C_ad^(r)/2.",
  "correction_to_expected_resolution": "The expected form of cross-class point (1) holds with two amendments: (a) O_c^(r,d) and O_g^(r,d) are NOT b_d-closed (b_d O_c^(r,d) = b_d O_g^(r,d) = Delta_1^(r)); only O_A^(d), (O_g - O_c)^(d) and the source-free invariants are; the non-invariant part of delta S^(1) is therefore E_A^(r), E_H AND the source counterterms with coefficient K_r + Gamma_r = -C_ad^(r)/2 (Q_R^(fr), Q_sigma^(W), Q_zeta, Q_rho[fg]); (b) the fermion loops do not populate barred copies Obar_A, Obar_g, Obar_c separately (Obar_A is not b_d-closed: b_d Qbar_(rho partial) contains the barred-only gauge variation of the d-dimensional F^2); they populate only the source-free barred invariants -1/4 Fbar^2 (coefficient -2/3 S_F^(r)), |Dbar H|^2 (-Yt) and Q_lambda (+Y4), i.e. the 4d combination (O_A - O_g + O_c)/2 with coefficient -2/3 S_F."
